# SigNoz setup

Add a dedicated ClickHouse service named `clickhouse` in this module:

```yaml
name: clickhouse
version: 0.0.0
module: {{ .Module }}
agent:
  kind: codefly:service
  name: clickhouse
  publisher: codefly.dev
  version: 0.0.9
endpoints:
  - name: tcp
    api: tcp
    visibility: private
spec:
  database-name: signoz
  no-migration: true
  docker-image: ghcr.io/codefly-dev/service-signoz/clickhouse:25.12.5-1@sha256:a1a57d1d2ec9de0c7bba2e3b7aba52ec16773a0ba0b3b2230379e272f869484d
```

Set `CLICKHOUSE_USER=signoz` and a dedicated `CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD` in that service's local configuration. Set a random `SIGNOZ_TOKENIZER_JWT_SECRET` in this service's local secret configuration. For Kubernetes, map `CLICKHOUSE_DSN` (`tcp://user:password@clickhouse:9000`) and `SIGNOZ_TOKENIZER_JWT_SECRET` to externally managed Secret keys; the ClickHouse service maps the same username and password independently. The SigNoz migration workload owns its telemetry schemas; dashboard and alert provisioning belongs outside this runtime agent.
